Romhack Base: Majora's Mask
Timeline Placement: Not too long after Majora's Mask
Length: Short (4 Chapters)
Significance: Revisiting characters and places, as well as emotional closure

Synopsis:
In this game, you play as the Deku Butler, who has learned somehow of the existence of Termina's Triforce, and intends to use its wish-granting ability to restore his son from his death-like state.
Unfortunately, someone else has grabbed the Triforce first, and due to their imbalanced heart, the 3 Pieces of the Triforce now abide with 3 troublesome individuals who are quite unwilling to hand them over...

[1] The game begins in the Southern Swamp: Something was stolen from the Deku King, and the Butler is sent to find it, though it is nowhere to be found.
After searching the whole swamp, the Deku Butler is sent out of the Swamp to track the thief using a single clue left behind.
In Clock Town, it becomes apparent people are losing valuables left and right. The people also speak of two individuals who have suddenly gained strange new powers, and may be behind the thefts:
the greedy smith Zubora, and pirate leader Aveil.

[2] The Triforce of Power is encountered first: in the hand of Mountain Smithy Zubora (the small guy). With power that has gone to his head, he now dresses like a king (though with consistently poor fashion sense).
He has abandoned the forge for a palace (much to Smithy Gabora's unhappiness), and has pressed the gorons into being both palace servants and miners of precious metals for his pleasure.
Bring him to his senses to obtain the Triforce of Power!
2 new locations: Goron Mines and Zubora's Palace.

[3] The Triforce of Courage is located next: in the hand of Pirate Leader Aveil. With untempered courage, she commands her petty band of followers into dangerous waters in search of lost treasures.
Unfortunately her boldness stirs up monsters better left buried beneath the waves. The pirates fight you once or twice as you follow their trail.
Aveil isn't fought at the end, but rather talked into handing over the Triforce after her underlings convince her it'd be for the best.
2 new locations: Marooner's Archipelago and the Lost City of Stars.
Marooner's Archipelago is full of holes where the pirates dug for treasure, but found nothing. A sea monster may be encountered here.
The Lost City of Stars may be an underwater alien fortress inhabited by a scarier version of the Romani Ranch aliens.

[4] The final part of the Triforce, the Triforce of Wisdom, remains with the one who first found and touched Termina's Triforce, causing it to split: the thief, Sakon.
Throughout the game, Sakon steals more and more things... even some things of no particular value but that their owners cherished them.
After the Great Bay episode, Sakon gets revealed as the thief stealing everyone's things, and becomes Public Enemy #1.
Unfortunately, Sakon's hideout is impenetrable.
That is where you come in.
With 2 Triforce Pieces, you open the door... and find that his hideout has become a labyrinthine fortress of utmost cruelty and cunning.
People from other regions aid you in traversing the stronghold. (Captain Viscen? Grown-up Kafei? Zubora and Gabora? The Elder's Son? Romani? Aveil? The Beaver Brothers? Pamela? No one undead remains...)
(Various soldiers to be used as pawns on Sakon's oversized game boards?)
At the end of the hideout, after a stolen robot activated against you is defeated... Sakon isn't there!
Returning to Clock Town... Sakon has stolen the whole town! It floats in the air, and only the Deku Butler can climb up to challenge him.
Finally cornering him, Sakon puts on a powerful mask he found (not Majora's Mask) and attacks!
In the end, Sakon is defeated, everyone's belongings are returned to them, and the Deku Butler gets the full Triforce, his wish granted at last.

Items & Abilities:
Main tool: Butler's umbrella. Used for offense, defense, and traversal. Also can create wind?
Triforce Parts grant abilities. The Triforce of Power may grant fire resistance: that is, fire no longer kills the Butler with one touch.
The Triforce of Courage may grant some water specific ability: perhaps the ability to swim after bounces have been used up.
Other potential items: Empty Bottle, Mask of Scents, Candle, Magic Bubbles... Magic Belt (speed enhanced?)? Gold Dust Parasol?

